[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5790738333","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123717#issuecomment-5790738333","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123717","id":5790738333,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWSennQ","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-23T07:20:52Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T07:21:08Z","body":"Perhaps there was a misunderstanding in the core meeting; what I meant was that I'd like to see PRs that are _thematically consistent_, i.e. one PR for each type of change. For example, there could be one PR that is just setting `singleton` pointers to `nullptr` on deinit. These are the types of PRs that are easy to review and merge.\r\n\r\nStuff like the `JoltJobSystem::~JoltJobSystem`, the `shader_cache[0] = RID();`, or `DisplayServer::reset` introduce semantic changes that need to be reviewed separately (as evidenced by the failing CI).\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5790738333/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5797213843","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123717#issuecomment-5797213843","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123717","id":5797213843,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABWYp2kw","user":{"login":"kisg","id":406832,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNjgzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/406832?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg","html_url":"https://github.com/kisg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-23T15:00:02Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T15:00:02Z","body":"> Perhaps there was a misunderstanding in the core meeting; what I meant was that I'd like to see PRs that are _thematically consistent_, i.e. one PR for each type of change. For example, there could be one PR that is just setting `singleton` pointers to `nullptr` on deinit. These are the types of PRs that are easy to review and merge.\r\n> \r\n> Stuff like the `JoltJobSystem::~JoltJobSystem`, the `shader_cache[0] = RID();`, or `DisplayServer::reset` introduce semantic changes that need to be reviewed separately (as evidenced by the failing CI).\r\n\r\nSure, we will split up the PR as you ask.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5797213843/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5865855555","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123717#issuecomment-5865855555","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123717","id":5865855555,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABXaHaQw","user":{"login":"kisg","id":406832,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNjgzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/406832?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg","html_url":"https://github.com/kisg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-28T07:59:19Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T07:59:19Z","body":"@Ivorforce I will look at your review comments one by one, but in general: in LibGodot it cannot be assumed that Godot was completely started when the shutdown happens.\r\n\r\nThis sequence is completely valid:\r\n\r\n```\r\ninstance = libgodot_create_instance() // invokes only Main::setup() \r\nlibgodot_destroy_instance(instance)\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt is also a valid case, when start() cannot complete, e.g. due to the command line parameters specified in the create arguments, like wrong rendering / display configuration:\r\n\r\n```\r\ninstance = libgodot_create_instance() // invokes only Main::setup()\r\n\r\ninstance.start() // Invokes setup2(), but fails in the displayserver setup, returns early.\r\n\r\n// Client detects the error, and destroys the instance\r\nlibgodot_destroy_instance(instance)\r\n```\r\nIn such cases a lot of the internal state of the engine will be uninitialized, so the cleanup code needs to take that into account.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5865855555/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5880595877","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123717#issuecomment-5880595877","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123717","id":5880595877,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABXoLFpQ","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user